  "generated_text": "First, we find the magnitude of each complex number:\n\n\\[\n|12-9i| = \\sqrt{12^2 + (-9)^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 81} = \\sqrt{225} = 15\n\\]\n\n\\[\n|8+15i| = \\sqrt{8^2 + 15^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 225} = \\sqrt{289} = 17\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the property of magnitudes that states the magnitude of the product of two complex numbers is the product of their magnitudes:\n\n\\[\n|(12-9i)(8+15i)| = |12-9i| \\cdot |8+15i| = 15 \\cdot 17\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the product:\n\n\\[\n15 \\cdot 17 = 255\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the magnitude of the product of  \\((12-9i)(8+15i)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{255}\n\\]",
